00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:43,900
Mr. Ishiguro, have you ever found one of your books at a second -hand bookstore?

11
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:47,380
Yes, that kind of thing is difficult.

12
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:50,720
If they've got my book there, I think, well,

13
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:52,420
is an insult.

14
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:55,100
Somebody didn't want to keep my book.

15
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:59,280
But if it's not there, I feel it's an insult too.

16
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:02,840
I think, why aren't people exchanging my book?

17
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:04,820
Why isn't it in this store?

18
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:08,640
Does being a writer require a thick skin?

19
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:12,840
Yes. For example, my wife can be very harsh.

20
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:19,140
I began working on my latest book, The Buried Giant, in 2004.

21
00:01:19,320 --> 00:01:23,300
But I stopped after I showed my wife a little section.

22
00:01:23,980 --> 00:01:25,360
She thought it was rubbish.

23
00:01:25,980 --> 00:01:28,360
Even after you won a Booker Prize?

24
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:31,260
She's not intimidated at all.

25
00:01:31,260 --> 00:01:36,620
And she criticizes me in exactly the same way she did when I was first unpublished

26
00:01:36,620 --> 00:01:37,820
and I was starting.

27
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:41,480
But you would never compromise on your vision.

28
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:47,520
No, I wouldn't ever compromise on the essential, the ideas, or the themes.

29
00:01:47,980 --> 00:01:51,700
This isn't really what my wife is trying to criticize me about.

30
00:01:52,020 --> 00:01:53,820
It's always about execution.

31
00:01:54,780 --> 00:01:59,560
So why did you put your book, The Buried Giant, aside for so long?

32
00:02:00,260 --> 00:02:03,680
Apparently you started working on it over ten years ago.

33
00:02:04,220 --> 00:02:08,640
I've often stopped writing a and left it for a few years.

34
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:13,000
And by the time I come back to it, it may have changed.

35
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:16,200
my imagination has moved on.

36
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:21,220
And I can think of different contexts or a different way to do it.

37
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:27,400
What does it feel like when you finally finish a It's funny you ask that because I

38
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:29,900
never have this moment when I feel,

39
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:36,000
I've finished. I watch footballers at the end of the match, you know, the whistle

40
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:42,820
goes and they've won or Until then, they've been giving everything they have and at

41
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:44,580
that moment they know it's over.

42
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:46,920
It's funny for an author.

43
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:49,680
There's never a finishing whistle.

